  "solution": "Given:\n\n(10, 5, 65)\n\n(9, 8, 89)\n\nLogic: Third no. = [(First no. × Second no.) + (First no. + Second no.)]\n\n**(10, 5, 65) →**\n\n⇒ [(10 × 5) + (10 + 5)]\n\n⇒ (50 + 15) = 65\n\n**(9, 8, 89) →**\n\n⇒ [(9 × 8) + (9 + 8)]\n\n⇒ (72 + 17) = 89\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (12, 5, 89)\n\n⇒ [(12 × 5) + (12 + 5)]\n\n⇒ (60 + 17) = 77\n\n**2.** (11, 10, 128)\n\n⇒ [(11 × 10) + (11 + 10)]\n\n⇒ (110 + 21) = 131\n\n**3. (4, 5, 29)**\n\n⇒ [(4 × 5) + (4 + 5)]\n\n⇒ (20 + 9) =** 29**\n\n**4.** (8, 7, 98)\n\n⇒ [(8 × 7) + (8 + 7)]\n\n⇒ (56 + 15) = 71\n\nHere, **(4, 5, 29)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (3)\".",
